# Same key, new line number. `export const SB_KEY` moved it from line 24 to line 37 in the
# 0.5.0 health commit, and a gitleaks fingerprint is PINNED TO THE LINE, so the two entries
# above stopped matching and the push was blocked on a finding this file had already settled.
# Re-read 2026-09-20: it is an `sb_publishable_` key, the class Supabase designs to ship in
# public clients, and RLS is what scopes the read.
#
# Only the commit-less form is written here, deliberately. A commit-pinned fingerprint cannot
# be recorded in the commit it pins: writing the line changes the tree, which changes the SHA,
# which invalidates the line just written. The commit-less form is SHA stable and is what
# actually holds.
#
# Any future edit that moves this line needs its own entry. Do not answer that with a repo
# `.gitleaks.toml`: the global pre-push hook checks for one first, and a local file silently
# replaces the estate's stricter ruleset for this whole repo.
